[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Result
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m All 68 rows have a passing differential test in `tests/phase_c_errors.rs`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (33 tests), reinforced by `tests/nan_matrix.rs` (the exhaustive NaN/inf
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cross-product) and `tests/fuzz_differential.rs`. Every assertion is bit-exact
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`f32::to_bits`), so `+0.0` vs `-0.0` and differing NaN payloads/sign bits are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m failures, not passes. Coverage of the multi-way branches is *asserted*, not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m assumed: `row30_row34_cache_validity_predicate`, `row49_row50_row51_c22_degenerate`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `row52_to_row59_c23_all_branches_and_degenerate` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `row40_row41_row42_row43_row44_loop_exits` recompute the C's own predicates and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m fail if any branch was never taken.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Divergence found and fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m One real bug surfaced here — an entire *class* of bug, not a single case.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `MULSS`/`ADDSS`/`SUBSS`/`DIVSS` return their **destination** operand when both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m operands are QNaNs. The C is compiled at `-O0` (no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`), so gcc
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m emits one instruction per source operation with a fixed, per-expression choice of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m destination register — and that choice is frequently the *second* source operand
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (e.g. `c2Add` computes `b + a` at the instruction level; `c2Dot`'s second product
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m uses `b.y` as destination; `c2Witness`'s `den * u` uses `u`). LLVM at `-O2`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m commutes `fmul`/`fadd`, folds `fneg` into `fsub`, and SLP-vectorises the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lanes into `mulps`/`addps`. Every one of those rewrites is arithmetically
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m equivalent, and every one of them changes which NaN sign bit survives.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Since this library validates nothing — shape coordinates, radii and rotation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m components may all be `NaN` — those are reachable inputs. Two source-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m attempts to block the folds failed (LLVM re-derives `fneg` from a sign-bit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `xor`, and `black_box` does not constrain operand order), so the fix pins the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m instruction sequence: `src/lib.rs`'s `fp` module wraps `mulss`/`addss`/`subss`/
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `divss`/`xorps` in inline asm with an explicit destination operand, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2Mulvs`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Div`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2Add`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c22`, `c23`, `c2L`, `c2Witness` and `c2GJK` were transcribed to match gcc's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m object code one instruction at a time. A portable `#[cfg]` fallback keeps the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m crate building on non-x86-64 targets.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    159[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Affected functions before the fix: `c2MulrvT`, `c2Add` (and therefore `c2Mulxv`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2Witness`, `c2L`, `c2GJK`), `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Mulrv`, and both public
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entry points `c2GJK`/`gjk`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Deliberately excluded (documented, not silently skipped)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 20 and 21: an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` reaching `c2GJK` leaves its
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    166[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2Proxy` locals uninitialised, so the C then reads stack garbage. That is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    167[0m:[38;5;10m[49m genuine C undefined behaviour whose value depends on the caller's frame history
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    168[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and cannot be reproduced by any translation. The deterministic half of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    169[0m:[38;5;10m[49m contract — `c2MakeProxy` performs no write at all for any out-of-range type — is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    170[0m:[38;5;10m[49m asserted exhaustively instead (rows 1 and 22: `3`, `4`, `5`, `7`, `99`, `-1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    171[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `-2`, `-100`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, plus 3000 random out-of-range ints, against a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    172[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pre-poisoned caller-owned buffer).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    173[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    174[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A `cache->count` of 5 or more is also excluded: the C's seeding loop writes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    175[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `verts[4]`, which is past the end of `c2Simplex`'s four `c2sv` slots and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    176[0m:[38;5;10m[49m corrupts the caller's stack. Both implementations perform the identical
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    177[0m:[38;5;10m[49m out-of-bounds write, so there is nothing to distinguish; `count == 4` (row 31) is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    178[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the largest value that stays inside the struct and *is* tested, including the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    179[0m:[38;5;10m[49m aliased `iA[3]`/`iB[3]` reads that land on `iB[0]` and `div`.
